RECONSTRUCTION - check against the original before trusting it.

The macOS dylibs vendored in third_party/brainflow-cerelog were built from
Shared_brainflow-cerelog 932b3944 plus an UNCOMMITTED change to
src/board_controller/cerelog/cerelog.cpp that was never pushed. VENDORED.md
describes it only as: "sets the re-opened serial port to raw mode with a 1 s
read timeout in connect_v1". This patch re-creates that behaviour from the
description, using the fork's own OSSerial::set_serial_port_settings
(src/utils/os_serial.cpp, POSIX branch): raw 8N1 (c_lflag=0, c_oflag=0,
CS8|CREAD|CLOCAL), VMIN=0, VTIME=ms_timeout/100 = 10 (1 s), then tcflush.
It runs before set_custom_baudrate, which on Linux uses TCGETS2/TCSETS2
(BOTHER) and on macOS tcgetattr/tcsetattr, so both keep the raw flags and
the timeout and change only the speed. connect_v2 already makes the same
call; this mirrors it. If the original diff turns up, diff it against this.

Apply from the repository root:  git apply cerelog-serial-timeout.patch
                              or  patch -p1 < cerelog-serial-timeout.patch

diff --git a/src/board_controller/cerelog/cerelog.cpp b/src/board_controller/cerelog/cerelog.cpp
index 8a038d5..f0e78b4 100644
--- a/src/board_controller/cerelog/cerelog.cpp
+++ b/src/board_controller/cerelog/cerelog.cpp
@@ -181,6 +181,18 @@ int Cerelog_X8::connect_v1 (const std::string &port_path)
         return (int)BrainFlowExitCodes::UNABLE_TO_OPEN_PORT_ERROR;
     }
 
+    // Raw 8N1 with a 1 s read timeout (VMIN=0, VTIME=10) on the re-opened port. Left at the
+    // OS defaults (canonical mode, blocking reads) the verification read below can block for
+    // minutes on a board that is not a V1, instead of failing over to the V2 strategy.
+    // Must run before set_custom_baudrate: it sets 115200, the custom baud call then overrides
+    // only the speed and keeps the raw flags and timeout.
+    if (serial->set_serial_port_settings (1000, false) < 0)
+    {
+        safe_logger (spdlog::level::err, "Failed to configure re-opened serial port.");
+        serial->close_serial_port ();
+        return (int)BrainFlowExitCodes::BOARD_WRITE_ERROR;
+    }
+
     safe_logger (spdlog::level::info, "Setting host to target baud rate: {}", info.baudrate);
     if (serial->set_custom_baudrate (info.baudrate) < 0)
     {
